<main class="policy faq-list"><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
<details><summary>Who can register?</summary><p>Attendees book events. Organisers register separately, submit private verification documents and require administrator approval to manage events and posts.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I find events?</summary><p>Search events, career categories and hashtags. Listings support location, category, format, dates, price and ticket-type filters. Hashtags can be clicked and searched; they cannot be followed.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why can I not book a particular event?</summary><p>An event may restrict career field, verified email domain or age. Student tickets require a temporary institutional email ending in .ac.za or tuks.co.za. These checks run on the server.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do tickets and payments work?</summary><p>Ticket tiers are General, VIP, Early Bird and Student. Free bookings bypass PayFast. Paid bookings stay pending until a verified sandbox notification. Pending reservations expire after four minutes; retry payment uses the existing pending booking.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I cancel or get a refund?</summary><p>Attendee cancellation requires more than 24 hours before the event. Local cancellation does not itself complete a provider refund. Paid cancellations and canceled events require support/payment-provider review.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do posts and feedback work?</summary><p>Verified organisers create text, image or video posts linked to an event. Attendees use thumbs up, applause or lightbulb reactions. There are no public comments. Reviews are private to the organiser and authorised admins.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if an event is problematic?</summary><p>Choose Report event from the event or your bookings. Support receives an email and investigates; reporting does not automatically prove fraud or issue a refund.</p></details>
